---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---

<DocsLayout
	title="Chaos Monkey"
	eyebrow="[ 05 · FUZZ ]"
	description="Type-aware fuzzing for Soroban — not random dumb bytes. Simulate first; broadcast only when preflight proceeds."
>
	<Callout type="warn" title="Real Testnet transactions">
		<p>
			Vectors whose simulation succeeds are signed with an ephemeral Friendbot-funded
			keypair and submitted on-chain. Keypairs are never written to disk or logged.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h2>Execution model</h2>
	<pre><code>vector → simulate (preflight)
           ├─ simulation fails    → classify from diagnostic events (nothing sent)
           └─ simulation succeeds → sign → broadcast → poll → classify</code></pre>

	<p>
		Many findings are therefore classified <em>without</em> an on-chain transaction. Only
		broadcast txs appear in verification samples and explorer links.
	</p>

	<h2>Design constraint</h2>
	<p>
		<strong>Type-correct ≠ semantically valid.</strong> A random <code>Address</code> is not
		a funded account, token, or authorized signer. Kuyfi classifies conservatively and treats
		ambiguity as ambiguity — see <a href={withBase('/findings')}>Findings</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Five vector families</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Family</th>
				<th>Module</th>
				<th>What it probes</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td>Math / boundary</td>
				<td><code>fuzzer_math.ts</code></td>
				<td>
					Per-type boundaries (<code>ZERO</code>, <code>MAX_I128</code>, empty/oversized
					bytes/strings, recursive UDT fields one-at-a-time).
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Authorization</td>
				<td><code>fuzzer_access.ts</code></td>
				<td>
					<code>UNAUTHORIZED_CALL</code>, <code>REINIT_ATTACK</code>,
					<code>SELF_CALL_ATTACK</code> on admin-named functions;
					<code>UNAUTHORIZED_ADDR_CALL</code> on Address params.
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Call ordering</td>
				<td><code>fuzzer_call_order.ts</code></td>
				<td>
					Same function twice: reinit / repeated withdraw / claim sequences matched by name.
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Fee / BPS</td>
				<td><code>fuzzer_fee.ts</code></td>
				<td>
					<code>BPS_*</code> boundaries (0, 1, 9999, 10000, 10001, type max) on fee-shaped
					params.
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Liquidity ratio</td>
				<td><code>fuzzer_liquidity.ts</code></td>
				<td>
					Paired extremes (<code>ZERO_A_MAX_B</code>, …) on swap/reserve-shaped functions.
				</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2>Session lifecycle (<code>runChaosMonkey</code>)</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Generate ephemeral keypair + Friendbot fund + on-chain confirmation.</li>
		<li>Connect Testnet RPC.</li>
		<li>
			Per discovered function: math, access, fee, liquidity fuzzers (each self-gates on
			name/params).
		</li>
		<li>Once per session: call-ordering candidates.</li>
		<li>Aggregate <code>ChaosReport</code> — <code>SECURE</code> / <code>PRECONDITION_FAIL</code> filtered from findings list, kept in counters.</li>
	</ol>

	<h2>Key modules</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><code>keypair_factory.ts</code> — ephemeral keys, never persisted</li>
		<li><code>type_gen.ts</code> — baseline + attack <code>ScVal</code>s from XDR types</li>
		<li><code>router.ts</code> — <code>invokeContract()</code> lifecycle; never throws, always typed <code>InvokeResult</code></li>
		<li><code>trace_analyzer.ts</code> — AUTH / CONTRACT / CONTEXT / OBJECT / STORAGE / WASM_VM / …</li>
		<li><code>result_parser.ts</code> — maps traces → VulnerabilitySignal + Severity</li>
		<li><code>reporter.ts</code> — <code>KYF-NNN</code> IDs, verification transaction sample</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Fixtures</h2>
	<p>
		Repo <code>test-fixtures/</code> includes an intentionally vulnerable access-control
		contract and a composite UDT fixture for controlled Testnet demos — not production code.
	</p>
</DocsLayout>
